{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"kunzite-bronzy-pachyderm","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe generated configuration reference contains an unsupported MCP exposure claim and lacks public descriptions for emitted settings. Hand-authored configuration guidance also contains stale ADR references and diagnostic-switch state. `consensual-ignored-ivorygull` records the accepted generator design. ADR 0086 and ADR 0087 provide current decision references.\n\n## Plan\n- Complete three bounded child tasks for generator narrative, setting descriptions, and current-state guidance.\n- Preserve generator ownership of `docs/config-reference.md`.\n- Keep each child behavior-neutral.\n- Do not create an MCP configuration tool.\n- Do not decide the deferred F05 generated-artifact catalog.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] F19A removes the nonexistent MCP configuration-surface claim through the generator.\n- [ ] F19B provides one generated public description for every emitted typed setting.\n- [ ] F19C corrects ADR references and diagnostic-switch guidance.\n- [ ] Generated files remain source-owned and drift checked.\n- [ ] All children pass applicable targeted checks and land independently.","id":"66c6-2fe5-4850-4297","parent_id":"f7e4-4d33-f231-4774","priority":1,"tags":["documentation","f19","configuration"],"ticket_type":"story","title":"F19 correct the generated configuration contract"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787417243601206001,"uuid":"b0f946d8-9732-487d-b11c-f21f99470480"}